  {
    q: 'Is FCL or LCL better for shipping to Oman?',
    a: 'Run the crossover arithmetic, then decide: $1,750 ÷ $190 ≈ 9 CBM at the cheap end of LCL, and $2,500 ÷ $110 ≈ 23 CBM at the expensive end. The band is wide because both inputs are LOW-confidence aggregates, so request FCL and LCL all-in quotes at the same destination and compare the full landed cost. LCL also adds consolidation, minimum charges and more destination handling.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is Oman’s tax cheaper than the UAE’s?',
    a: 'No — it is identical. Oman’s statutory stack and the UAE’s both compound 5% duty with 5% VAT to ×1.1025, so a $10,000 CIF lands at $11,025 in either market: a $0 tax difference. The real Oman-vs-UAE differences show up in the freight lane (sailings, consolidation volume, port choice), not in the tax code. Saudi Arabia is the expensive comparison at ×1.2075 ($12,075).',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which Omani port should be used in the quote?',
    a: 'Sohar (OMSOH) is the container gateway for Muscat and northern Oman. Salalah (OMSLL) serves southern Oman demand and transshipment relays. Note that Muscat city itself has no commercial container seaport any more — Port Sultan Qaboos shifted to cruise operations and cargo moved to Sohar, so a quote naming “Muscat port” for discharge is really a sea-plus-truck move. State the exact discharge point on the bill of lading.',
