  <section class="section container">
    <h2>Key takeaways</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Tax parity is exact: Oman’s ×1.1025 (5% duty, then 5% VAT on the $10,500 base) matches the UAE to the cent — $11,025 on $10,000 CIF, with $25 of it born from compounding; Saudi Arabia is $1,050 heavier and Qatar/Kuwait $525 lighter.</li>
      <li>The first published Oman lane rows are LOW confidence: 20ft FCL $1,750–$2,500, 40ft $2,110–$3,680, LCL $110–$190/CBM, air $2.40–$3.50/kg — planning floors, not quotes.</li>
      <li>The small-market signal is clearest at the LCL floor: $110 ÷ $30 (UAE base) ≈ 3.7×; against the corridor-wide $20 floor it is 5.5×. FCL ordering between Oman and the UAE stays UNKNOWN across the available sources.</li>
      <li>The crossover is a band, not a number: $1,750–$2,500 ÷ $110–$190 = roughly 9–23 CBM, so FCL logic arrives earlier than the usual 15 CBM habit on this lane.</li>
      <li>Muscat has no container seaport: commercial cargo moved to Sohar (Port Sultan Qaboos now caters mainly to cruise liners), so confirm OMSOH or OMSLL on the bill of lading and price the inland leg.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="section container">
    <h2>The Author's Take</h2>
    <p><strong>Position:</strong> In my view, “same ×1.1025 as the UAE” is exactly the line that gets Oman mis-priced — the tax is identical to the cent, but the published LCL floor runs about 3.7× the UAE’s and the FCL rows cannot even be compared across confidence levels, so I price Oman as a friction lane and refuse to book it on tax logic.</p>
    <ul><li>$110 ÷ $30 ≈ 3.7× at the LCL floor — the one comparison the floors can carry without a confidence mismatch.</li><li>Oman’s FCL rows are LOW-confidence aggregates; the UAE’s are HIGH-confidence spot. The ordering is UNKNOWN, so force two quotes onto one basis before believing any premium or discount story.</li><li>The crossover band runs 9–23 CBM ($1,750–$2,500 ÷ $110–$190) — wide enough that a fixed 15 CBM habit cannot decide it, so quote both inside the band.</li></ul>
    <p class="note"><em>Disclosure: This is the author's editorial judgment based on the published data on this page — not an independently verified fact.</em></p>
  </section>

